# What the image build must not copy. The Dockerfile runs `COPY . .`, so
# without this file a build from a tree that holds a working .env bakes the
# provider key into the image's /app/.env, where anyone who pulls or saves the
# image can read it. Found 2026-11-17 by a cold start from the README: an
# image built from the owner's tree on 2026-11-16 carried a 3.4 KB /app/.env,
# and the README said to put the key in .env and then build. The key reaches
# the container through `--env-file` at run time, not through the image.
.env*
!.env.example

# Local state and scratch that is not source.
.git
.venv
venv
*.db
*.sqlite3
chromadb_data
evals/results
*.log
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
*.egg-info
.claude
.qwen
ai-native-starter-pack
docs/milkhouse
docs/private*
evals/private*
profiles/milkhouse.yaml
